ScenePlates sets a table of plants (or any uses) as a ruled ledger beside one navy drawing plate: the plant you point at, focus or choose is drawn on the plate as one water header with a drop to each of its points of use, numbered as the ledger's "where the water goes" list.

- On the site: a `table` block with `"look": "scene-plates"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-scene-plates.js`); ind-process.2 "Food, beverage and cannabis". Origin: pass 12 build B, concept `design-system/inspiration/gemini/218-p12-ind-process-food.png` (a ledger beside a navy plate: a proofing tank fed by a drop, numbered callouts). Not copied: its two generic skid thumbnails and its mono ledger. A sibling of SitePlates (a sites ledger, contact-locations), which stays as it is: SitePlates has no plant scenes and showed an empty plate here.
- Data: `cols` [plant, where the water goes, legal floor and limit, fit]; `rows`: the first cell names the plant (a `{t, link}` cell links it); the second is split at ", " (never inside brackets) into the numbered uses; the third prints each " · " part on its own line (the floor, then who sets the rest, muted); the fourth is a plain or `{t, link}` cell. `fold`, `fold_noun` as everywhere (folded rows are `tr.aq-fold-x`). `nav` (optional) prints under the title with the count ("Food and beverage · 04", aria-hidden).
- Optional `art` (look-only): per row, one station key per use: `proof` (proofing tank, IsoKit tank), `batch` (mixing kettle with agitator), `lab` (laboratory sink, IsoKit outlet), `boiler` (horizontal boiler on saddles with its stack), `line` (filling line: conveyor, bottles, filler head). Without `art` each use picks its station from its words: proofing, lab, boiler, product lines or touches the product, else a batch kettle.
- Markup: `div.aq-scene-plates` (`data-pk-sticky`, `data-pk-h="220"`) → `div.__main` (head, the table, folded or not; the block's `nav` label is not printed, it is the page-nav label) and `div.__side` → `div.__plate` (`data-theme="dark"`, `aria-hidden="true"`: the ledger carries every fact, so screen readers never hear a plant twice; `data-pk-fig`) → `div.__reel` of `figure.__still` (`--d` its distance from the plant in hand): `figcaption.__cap` (`__ci` index, `__ck` plant), `div.__area` > `div.__fig` (`--ar`, the IsoKit svg `aq-iso--navy` and `span.__pin` numbers), `ol.__calls`. Rows: `tr.__row` (`data-i`, `data-pk-row`) with `th` > `div.__plant` (`button.__pick` index, 44 × 44 px, `aria-pressed`; `span.__name`), `td.__where` > `ol.__uses` (`__un` number), `td.__limit` (`span.__ln`, `__ln--then`), `td.__fit`; each `td` carries `data-l` (its column head) for narrow widths.
- Desktop: ledger 7 parts, plate 5, the plate held in view (sticky) while the ledger scrolls. Ledger in sans 14/21 on hairlines; the row in hand has a `flow` rule at its foot, its index in `flow` and its use numbers filled `navy`. The plate: index and plant, the drawing (the stations stand in a staggered row, a gap along x and a gap back along y, so the row reads level across the plate and a phone strip draws it wide; one header steps back behind them with an arrow where it comes in, a drop to each station, numbered pins), the numbered callouts. 861–1,100 px: the rows become cards with their column heads as small labels.
- Selection: pointing at a row, focusing into it or pressing its index slides the reel (240 ms, cubic-bezier(.2,.85,.25,1); instant for keyboard and reduced motion); the choice persists.
- **Phones** (≤ 860 px): title, then the plate as a 220 px navy strip held under the header (PhoneKit sticky figure; caption and drawing, callouts left to the rows) that swaps to the plant whose row is on the reading line, then the rows as cards: index and plant (17/23), the uses as numbered chips keyed to the strip's pins, floor and limit, fit, all 14/21. Column labels show on the first card only (S12; kept for screen readers on the others). Height at 375: 1,624 px (site-plates here: 1,952). The strip drawing fills the strip width (344 px at 375, 394 px at 768).
- Tokens: `navy` plate with `on-navy` and `on-navy-muted`, drawing `aq-iso--navy`; ledger `ink`, `ink-muted`, `line`, `line-strong`, `flow`.
- Not for sites with addresses and contacts (use SitePlates) or for more than about six stations per plant.

## Motion

The header rule draws across and the rows rise in; the plate wipes in from the right, the plant in hand is drawn on it (AQiso: lines back to front, then the water along the main and down each drop), its pins strike in order and the callouts follow; once on scroll-in, under 3 s. Choosing another plant: the reel slides and the arriving pins strike. The reel is ported from Subframe Motion "Hover image preview list" (project-index), MIT, (c) 2026 Subframe; the entry pattern is SitePlates'. Reduced motion: the finished state.
